@copilot Add the following explanatory source comment immediately above the explicit span-name extractor initialization cast in `instrumentation/apache-dubbo-2.7/library-autoconfigure/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/apachedubbo/v2_7/DubboTelemetryBuilder.java`, and above both equivalent client/server casts in `instrumentation/thrift-0.13/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/thrift/v0_13/internal/ThriftInstrumenterFactory.java`:

```java
// Initialize before customization: a user-provided wrapper may hide the RPC extractor
// from InstrumenterBuilder's automatic initialization.
```

The comment explains why the original RPC span-name extractor must be initialized before a user-provided customizer can wrap it and hide its internal initialization interface. Apply the approved wording at all three sites. This is a comment-only change: retain the existing casts, initialization order, public APIs, and behavior. Do not refactor the getter constructor or initialization design, and do not make unrelated changes. Commit and push to this existing PR's head branch and preserve its current draft/ready state. Do not reply to real-user review comments or resolve threads.

